### Assignment CRUD API – Test Requests
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or import into Postman

@base = http://localhost:5000/api/assignments

### ── 1. CREATE Assignment (POST) ────────────────────────────────
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Data Structures Lab Report",
  "description": "Implement Stack and Queue using linked list in C++",
  "subject": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
  "studentName": "Rahul Sharma",
  "department": "Computer Science & Engineering",
  "dueDate": "2025-05-15",
  "status": "Pending"
}

### ── 2. READ ALL Assignments (GET) ──────────────────────────────
GET {{base}}

### ── 2a. READ with filters ──────────────────────────────────────
GET {{base}}?status=Pending&department=Computer Science %26 Engineering

### ── 3. READ ONE Assignment by ID (GET) ─────────────────────────
# Replace <id> with actual MongoDB _id from create response
GET {{base}}/<id>

### ── 4. UPDATE Assignment (PUT) ─────────────────────────────────
PUT {{base}}/<id>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Submitted",
  "marks": 88
}

### ── 5. DELETE Assignment (DELETE) ──────────────────────────────
DELETE {{base}}/<id>
